(go/type ClientSessionCache "ClientSessionCache is a cache of ClientSessionState objects that can be used\nby a client to resume a TLS session with a given server. ClientSessionCache\nimplementations should expect to be called concurrently from different\ngoroutines. Up to TLS 1.2, only ticket-based resumption is supported, not\nSessionID-based resumption. In TLS 1.3 they were merged into PSK modes, which\nare supported via this interface.\n" (interface


    (^{:doc "Get searches for a ClientSessionState associated with the given key.\nOn return, ok is true if one was found.\n"} Get [^string sessionKey] :results [^{:tag (* ClientSessionState)} session ^bool ok])





    (^{:doc "Put adds the ClientSessionState to the cache with the given key. It might\nget called multiple times in a connection if a TLS 1.3 server provides\nmore than one session ticket. If called with a nil *ClientSessionState,\nit should remove the cache entry.\n"} Put [^string sessionKey ^{:tag (* ClientSessionState)} cs])))


